In article <1992Oct20.225830.251@u.washington.edu>, angus@hardy.u.washington.edu (Angus the Demonchild) writes:
|> Well, there are more ways than one to acquire Aggravate Monster.  One
|> obvious way is to eat the corpse of a human or were-human ('You
|> Cannibal!  You'll regret this!').  Another is to wear a ring of
|> aggravate monster.  One not so obvious way to contract Aggravate
|> Monster is to fail while reading a spellbook.  If you see the message
|> 'You feel threatened.', you've got it.
|> 
|> I'm sure there are one or two other ways that I might have forgotten.

I think the spoiler file may be wrong on this.  It says that when you 
get the "you feel threatened" message, (either from sitting on a throne
of from attempting to read a spell book) you get the aggravate monster
intinsic.

I just looked at the code, and I don't think that's true.  It seems to
aggravate all the sleeping monsters around you, but not give you the
intrinsic -- just a one shot deal.

From what I could find in the code, the only way to get the intrinsic
is to eat either a human corpse (an elf corpse if you're an Elf), or a
dog/cat corpse.  All the other ways mentioned in the spoilers seem
to only aggravate monster currently around you (like when you read
a cursed scare monster scroll).

I haven't checked out all the ways mentioned in the spoilers, but you 
don't seem to get it from failing to read a spell book.

